aurant keeps getting the same complaint online; the owner insists it is malice, but the inspector books a visit anyway.</li><li>A politician denies a story four times in a week and the press get more interested, not less.</li></ul><p>ES: Cuando el río suena, agua lleva.</p><p>The Catalan and Spanish use water, English uses fire — worth two minutes on why. Pairs with the unit's speculation and unsolved mysteries.</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"nmv97qyzabla41.0","section":"homework","kind":"text","title":"Waiting room – Vocabulary game","html":"","link":"https://as1-design.github.io/improvedlessons/waiting-room-B21.html","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false}]}],"sections":[{"id":"warmup","label":"Warm up","emoji":"🔥"},{"id":"memory","label":"Let’s take a walk down memory lane…","emoji":"🛤️"},{"id":"speaking","label":"Speaking zone","emoji":"🗣️"},{"id":"activities","label":"Activities","emoji":"🎯"},{"id":"phrase","label":"Phrase of the day","emoji":""},{"id":"wrapup","label":"Wrap up","emoji":"✍️"},{"id":"homework","label":"Homework","emoji":"📚"},{"id":"tasks","label":"This week online","emoji":"💻"},{"id":"answers","label":"Answer key","emoji":"🔑"},{"id":"notes","label":"Teacher notes","emoji":"📝"}],"emojis":{"warmup":"🔥","memory":"🛤️","speaking":"🗣️","activities":"🎯","phrase":"","wrapup":"✍️","homework":"📚","tasks":"💻","answers":"🔑","notes":"📝"},"generated":"2026-10-15T07:24:44.930Z"}